    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d336">

                <pb facs="0456" n="354" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg354"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/4978</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-07-07"><hi rendition="#italic">July 7,
                        1927</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received August 9.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 437</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transcribe herewith for
                    the information of the Department, the Decree No. 49 of President Diaz calling
                    elections in the Departments and Districts where no such elections were held in
                    1926 on account of revolution:</p>
                <p rendition="#center">(From <hi rendition="#italic">La Gaceta</hi>, Diario Oficial,
                    Managua, June 18, 1927)</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>A translation of this Decree follows:</p>
                <p rendition="#center">No. 49</p>
                <p>The President of the Republic in the use of his powers and in accord with Article
                    81 of the Constitution,</p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Decrees</hi>: <list>
                        <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> 1st: Call elections of
                            Senators and Deputies in those departments and districts where on
                            account of war such elections were not held or remain incomplete.</item>
                        <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> 2nd: This Decree also affects
                            the districts and cantons of the Atlantic Coast where there was no
                            voting because those places were occupied by the rebel forces.</item>
                        <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> 3rd: Sunday, the Fourth of
                            September of the current year, is set for the day to carry into effect
                            this voting.</item>
                        <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> 4th: This Decree will
                            commence to be in force from the date of its insertion in the <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Gazette</hi>, and in the Departments of Leon,
                            Chinandega, Estelí and Bluefields from its proclamation by Band in the
                            capitals of such departments.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>Make public. Presidency. Managua, June 17, 1927. Adolfo Diaz. Minister of the
                    Interior, Ricardo Lopez C.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles C.
                    Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
